<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    The app's entitlements.

    This file was an empty dict for as long as the build signed with a free personal team, which
    can grant none of these: an entitlement a team cannot grant is a SIGNING failure rather than a
    runtime one, so they were absent instead of requested. A paid Apple Developer Program
    membership now exists — App Store Connect holds the app record — so the two this app actually
    needs are requested again. Config.xcconfig carries the full history and the two that stay out.

    aps-environment
        Required for ANY push on iOS. FirebaseMessaging and kmpNotifier are already wired in
        iOSApp.swift and in the shared code, and without this line they have no APNs token to
        register, so IP-157's push half was dead on iPhone while the in-app inbox (which polls
        GET /api/me/notifications over plain HTTP and needs no entitlement) kept working.

        The value is `development` on purpose. Xcode substitutes `production` when it exports an
        archive against a distribution profile, which is what a TestFlight or App Store build is,
        so writing `production` here would only break the debug build on a cable.

        Firebase also needs an APNs authentication key (.p8) uploaded to the monad-count project,
        or the token is registered and no message is ever delivered.

    com.apple.developer.associated-domains
        Two claims on one domain, both already served by monad.dubec.dev:

          applinks:        a printed marker scanned with the CAMERA app opens the app instead of
                           Safari. The claimed paths are /d/* (fleet device labels) and /m/* (lab
                           marker cards); the in-app scanner never depended on this.
          webcredentials:  a password saved for monad.dubec.dev is offered on the login screen and
                           saved back under the domain's name rather than an opaque bundle id.

        The domain's half of both claims is
        /.well-known/apple-app-site-association, served by monad_knowledge.web.routes.applinks.
        IT IS AN EMPTY CLAIM UNTIL `web.applinks.ios_app_ids` IS SET IN config.toml AND THE SITE IS
        RELEASED. An empty claim fails silently on the handset, so check the served file before
        blaming the entitlement.

    Live Activities need nothing here. The check-in widget is started and updated by the app itself
    (MonadPresenceBridge), not pushed to, so it works on any signing path.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:monad.dubec.dev</string>
		<string>webcredentials:monad.dubec.dev</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
